bx uses libc regex. On libc without REG_STARTEND, regex operations on
input containing NUL fail rather than silently matching truncated lines.
-i takes an optional attached suffix (-i.bak); -i alone and -i '' both
mean no backup. -I retains FreeBSD's required argument. In-place editing
rejects symlinks, uses mkstemp in the same directory, preserves owner,
group and ordinary permission bits, and drops set-id bits. Backup creation
requires hard-link support. This is not GNU sed; no shell execution or
GNU long options are provided.
